g-warp obsolet
use guile ffi
or nyacc  ffi-helper



	David Pirotte david@altosw.be via gnu.org 
	to  guile-devel, guile-user
	> ...
	> For new projects likely. Is there a simple update-path for projects
	> currently using g-wrap?

	The simple update path is to drop any g-wrap generated bindings, then
	read the nyacc ffi-helper doc, which comes with examples as well, then
	write a simple module to be compiled as recommended by nyacc ffo-helper
	(not gona repeat this here), then use those bindings and/or provide a
	higher level api ...

	They are quite a few projects 'out there' using this approach, fwiw
	guile-fluidsynth is one of them -  which I maintain

		https://cgit.git.savannah.nongnu.org/cgit/guile-fluidsynth.git/tree/

